        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fdf34017-2fe4-570f-91bc-33e0b3d7f460",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: João Paulo II Airport, São Miguel, Azores\n- Organizations: SATA Group, SATA Air Açores, Azores Airlines, Ryanair\n- People: Pope John Paul II\n- Topics: airport hubs, airline traffic rankings\n\nFacts:\n- João Paulo II Airport is an international airport on the island of São Miguel in the Portuguese archipelago of the Azores.\n- João Paulo II Airport has the IATA code PDL and the ICAO code LPPD.\n- João Paulo II Airport is named after Pope John Paul II.\n- João Paulo II Airport is the major hub for the SATA Group of airlines, including SATA Air Açores and Azores Airlines.\n- Since April 2015, João Paulo II Airport has served as a base for Ryanair.\n- In 2016, Ryanair was the largest European airline by scheduled passengers flown.\n- In 2016, Ryanair carried more international passengers than any other airline.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
